    <KeyTakeaway text="New York's 480-a Forest Tax Law program allows qualifying woodland owners with 50 or more contiguous acres to reduce property and school taxes by up to 80% of the assessed value of enrolled acreage — in exchange for a 10-year commitment to follow a DEC-approved forest management plan written by a certified forester." />

